{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     page/statement — a page that opens with a statement rather than a heading.
     Shape from NSDS templates/personal-site.html.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     Takes one partial parameter:  {{> "page/statement" slug="about"}}

     ── WHY IT HAS TO FETCH ITS OWN PAGE ────────────────────────────────────
     A CONTENT-LESS static route in routes.yaml binds NO post. Ghost's own
     comment on those routes says the template "also works if a Ghost page
     with the matching slug exists" — it does not. The page is not passed in,
     {{#post}} resolves to nothing, and the template renders an empty <main>:
     chrome, footer, and a hole where the page was. Verified in production —
     /about/ and /sponsor/ returned 200 and rendered nothing at all.

     So when there is no post in context, the slug names the page and this
     goes and gets it. The slug is not a guess: page-about.hbs is BY NAME the
     template for /about/, which is the whole reason a file with that name
     exists (see its header).

     ⚠ THE FETCH IS THE FALLBACK, NOT THE PATH. When Ghost DOES supply the
     page — a normal page render, or a route corrected to `data: page.about` —
     {{#post}} wins and no query runs. Fixing routes.yaml in Admin therefore
     makes this branch dead rather than wrong, which is the right way round.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
{{#post}}
    {{> "page/statement-body"}}
{{else}}
    {{#get "pages" filter="slug:{{slug}}" limit="1" as |pages|}}
        {{#if pages}}
            {{#foreach pages}}{{> "page/statement-body"}}{{/foreach}}
        {{else}}
            {{!-- ⚠ A ROUTE THAT OUTLIVED ITS PAGE. /sponsor/ and
                 /become-author/ are both in the live routes.yaml and neither
                 has a Ghost page behind it any more — verified against the
                 Content API, which lists eight pages and neither of those.

                 Ghost cannot 404 a route that exists, so without this the URL
                 answers 200 with a blank column, and abstract/collections.md
                 is explicit that a blank column reads as a broken page. An
                 empty state at least tells the truth.

                 THE REAL FIX IS NOT HERE. Either write the page in Ghost
                 Admin, or drop the route from Admin → Labs → Routes so the
                 URL can 404 honestly. A 200 on a URL with nothing behind it
                 is worth removing rather than decorating. --}}
            {{> "empty" title=(t "Nothing here yet")
                        text=(t "This page has not been written.")}}
        {{/if}}
    {{/get}}
{{/post}}
